More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (521–530)
521. Improper Validation of API Export Functions
API Data Export Exposure
Export endpoints allow attackers to download large amounts of sensitive user data.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $8,000
522. Insecure Handling of User Role Assignments
Privilege Escalation via Role Manipulation
Attackers manipulate role parameters to gain higher privileges.
💰 Typical payout: $700 – $12,000
523. Improper Validation of File Compression Formats
Archive Decompression Vulnerability
Applications decompress files without validation, allowing file overwrite or server compromise.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $8,000
524. Insecure Handling of API Authentication Headers
API Authentication Header Exposure
Sensitive authentication headers leak through logs or error responses.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
525. Improper Validation of Payment Callbacks
Payment Callback Manipulation
Attackers manipulate payment callback responses to mark transactions as successful.
💰 Typical payout: $1,000 – $15,000
526. Insecure Handling of WebSocket Authentication
WebSocket Authentication Bypass
Attackers connect to WebSocket channels without proper authentication.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
527. Improper Validation of Content Security Policy
Weak Content Security Policy
Weak CSP configurations allow attackers to execute malicious scripts.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
528. Insecure Handling of Mobile Push Notifications
Push Notification API Abuse
Attackers send fake push notifications to users or retrieve notification data.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
529. Improper Validation of URL Fragments
URL Fragment Injection
Applications incorrectly process URL fragments, allowing manipulation of client-side logic.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
530. Insecure Handling of API Access Tokens
API Access Token Leakage
Access tokens exposed in URLs, logs, or client-side code allow unauthorized access.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
